<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proofs</h2>

<section id="A3.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Proof for Proposition <a href="#Thmprop1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ Proof for Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ ARMOR: High-Performance Semi-Structured Pruning via Adaptive Matrix Factorization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="Thmprop1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmprop1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1</span></span><span id="Thmprop1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmprop1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmprop1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmprop1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The proxy loss is bounded below by <math id="Thmprop1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> and is convex with respect to <math id="Thmprop1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmprop1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmprop1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> individually. A formal proof is provided in Appendix <a href="#A3.SSx1" title="Proof for Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ ARMOR: High-Performance Semi-Structured Pruning via Adaptive Matrix Factorization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SSx1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proxy loss is defined as:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta)=||\overline{W}-\hat{W}||_{F,\text{diag}(XX^{T})}^{2}=\sum_{i,j}(\overline{W}_{ij}-\hat{W}_{ij})^{2}||X_{j}||_{2}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta)=||\overline{W}-\hat{W}||_{F,\text{diag}(XX^{T})}^{2}=\sum_{i,j}(\overline{W}_{ij}-\hat{W}_{ij})^{2}||X_{j}||_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SSx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{W}=A(W^{\prime}\odot M)B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{W}=A(W^{\prime}\odot M)B</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SSx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bounded Below by 0:</span>
For each term in the summation, <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\overline{W}_{ij}-\hat{W}_{ij})^{2}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\overline{W}_{ij}-\hat{W}_{ij})^{2}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> as it is a squared real number. The weighting term <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="||X_{j}||_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">||X_{j}||_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is the squared Euclidean norm of a vector, which is also non-negative. A sum of non-negative terms is non-negative. Thus, <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\hat{W})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\hat{W})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Convexity with respect to A:</span>
When B, <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and M are held fixed, let <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=(W^{\prime}\odot M)B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=(W^{\prime}\odot M)B</annotation></semantics></math>. The proxy loss function can be written as a function of A:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(A)=||\overline{W}-AS||_{F,D}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(A)=||\overline{W}-AS||_{F,D}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\text{diag}(XX^{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\text{diag}(XX^{T})</annotation></semantics></math>. This is a weighted least squares objective. The function <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(A)=\overline{W}-AS" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(A)=\overline{W}-AS</annotation></semantics></math> is an affine (linear) transformation of A. The function <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(Z)=||Z||_{F,D}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(Z)=||Z||_{F,D}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a squared weighted Frobenius norm, which is a convex function. The composition of a convex function with an affine transformation is convex. Therefore, the proxy loss is convex with respect to A.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Convexity with respect to B:</span>
Similarly, when A, <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and M are held fixed, let <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}=A(W^{\prime}\odot M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}=A(W^{\prime}\odot M)</annotation></semantics></math>. The proxy loss function can be written as a function of B:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(B)=||\overline{W}-S^{\prime}B||_{F,D}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(B)=||\overline{W}-S^{\prime}B||_{F,D}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This is also a weighted least squares objective. Using the same reasoning as for A, the function is a composition of a convex function (squared norm) with an affine transformation of B, and thus is convex with respect to B.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Convexity with respect to <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span>
When A, B, and M are held fixed, the reconstructed weight matrix <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{W}=A(W^{\prime}\odot M)B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{W}=A(W^{\prime}\odot M)B</annotation></semantics></math> is a linear function of the elements of <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\prime}=\text{vec}(W^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>vec</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\prime}=\text{vec}(W^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, the vector of elements in <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{vec}(\hat{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>vec</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{vec}(\hat{W})</annotation></semantics></math> is a linear transformation of <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. The objective function <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\hat{W})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\hat{W})</annotation></semantics></math> is a quadratic function of the elements of <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{W}</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore a quadratic function of the elements of <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, it is a positive semidefinite quadratic form, which is convex. Therefore, the proxy loss is convex with respect to <math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A3.SSx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Proof for Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1. ‣ Proof for Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ ARMOR: High-Performance Semi-Structured Pruning via Adaptive Matrix Factorization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The continuous parameter update step results in a equal or lower proxy loss:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{W,X}\left(\hat{W}\left((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t+1},(W^{\prime})_{t+1|\mathrm{cont}},(M)_{t}\right)\right)\leq\mathcal{L}_{W,X}\left(\hat{W}\left((A)_{t},(B)_{t},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t}\right)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>cont</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{W,X}\left(\hat{W}\left((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t+1},(W^{\prime})_{t+1|\mathrm{cont}},(M)_{t}\right)\right)\leq\mathcal{L}_{W,X}\left(\hat{W}\left((A)_{t},(B)_{t},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t}\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SSx2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SSx2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The paper states that the continuous optimization step updates the parameters A, B, and <math id="A3.SSx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> using sequential gradient descent (Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ B.2 Algorithm Pseudocode ‣ Appendix B ARMOR Optimization Algorithm in Depth ‣ ARMOR: High-Performance Semi-Structured Pruning via Adaptive Matrix Factorization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). The process is iterative:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SSx2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="A3.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Update A: <math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A)_{t+1}=(A)_{t}-\eta_{A}\nabla_{A}\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t},(B)_{t},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>A</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A)_{t+1}=(A)_{t}-\eta_{A}\nabla_{A}\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t},(B)_{t},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Update B: <math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(B)_{t+1}=(B)_{t}-\eta_{B}\nabla_{B}\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>B</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(B)_{t+1}=(B)_{t}-\eta_{B}\nabla_{B}\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Update <math id="A3.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A3.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W^{\prime})_{t+1|\mathrm{cont}}=(W^{\prime})_{t}-\eta_{W^{\prime}}\nabla_{W^{\prime}}\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t+1},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>cont</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W^{\prime})_{t+1|\mathrm{cont}}=(W^{\prime})_{t}-\eta_{W^{\prime}}\nabla_{W^{\prime}}\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t+1},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A3.SSx2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">From Proposition 1, the loss function <math id="A3.SSx2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{W,X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{W,X}</annotation></semantics></math> is convex with respect to each of A, B, and <math id="A3.SSx2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> individually. As Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ B.2 Algorithm Pseudocode ‣ Appendix B ARMOR Optimization Algorithm in Depth ‣ ARMOR: High-Performance Semi-Structured Pruning via Adaptive Matrix Factorization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> states, the learning rate <math id="A3.SSx2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is determined via local <math id="A3.SSx2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothness, which are calculated in <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Beta Smoothness of Proxy Loss ‣ ARMOR: High-Performance Semi-Structured Pruning via Adaptive Matrix Factorization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SSx2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SSx2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">For a convex and <math id="A3.SSx2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth function <math id="A3.SSx2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, the gradient descent update <math id="A3.SSx2.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{k+1}=x_{k}-\eta\nabla f(x_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{k+1}=x_{k}-\eta\nabla f(x_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> with a step size <math id="A3.SSx2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta\leq 1/\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta\leq 1/\beta</annotation></semantics></math> guarantees that <math id="A3.SSx2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x_{k+1})\leq f(x_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x_{k+1})\leq f(x_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SSx2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SSx2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Applying this property to each step of the sequential update:</span></p>
<ol id="A3.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The update of A ensures that</p>
<table id="A3.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t})\leq\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t},(B)_{t},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t})\leq\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t},(B)_{t},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The update of B, starting from the new A, ensures that</p>
<table id="A3.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t+1},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t})\leq\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t+1},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t})\leq\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The update of <math id="A3.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, starting from the new A and B, ensures that</p>
<table id="A3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t+1},(W^{\prime})_{t+1|\mathrm{cont}},(M)_{t})\leq\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t+1},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>cont</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t+1},(W^{\prime})_{t+1|\mathrm{cont}},(M)_{t})\leq\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t+1},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A3.SSx2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Chaining these inequalities together, we get:</span></p>
<table id="A3.SSx2.p4.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.SSx2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t+1},(W^{\prime})_{t+1|\mathrm{cont}},(M)_{t})\leq\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t+1},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t})\\
\leq\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t})\leq\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t},(B)_{t},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>cont</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t+1},(W^{\prime})_{t+1|\mathrm{cont}},(M)_{t})\leq\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t+1},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t})\\
\leq\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t})\leq\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((A)_{t},(B)_{t},(W^{\prime})_{t},(M)_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SSx2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SSx2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, each continuous optimization step is guaranteed to not increase the proxy loss.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SSx3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Proof for Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma C.2. ‣ Proof for Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ ARMOR: High-Performance Semi-Structured Pruning via Adaptive Matrix Factorization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The sparse core update step results in a equal or lower proxy loss:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{W,X}\left(\hat{W}\left((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t+1},(W^{\prime})_{t+1},(M)_{t+1}\right)\right)\leq\mathcal{L}_{W,X}\left(\hat{W}\left((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t+1},(W^{\prime})_{t+1|\mathrm{cont}},(M)_{t}\right)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>cont</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{W,X}\left(\hat{W}\left((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t+1},(W^{\prime})_{t+1},(M)_{t+1}\right)\right)\leq\mathcal{L}_{W,X}\left(\hat{W}\left((A)_{t+1},(B)_{t+1},(W^{\prime})_{t+1|\mathrm{cont}},(M)_{t}\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SSx3.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SSx3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The discrete optimization step (Algorithm 3) seeks to improve the sparse core <math id="A3.SSx3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}\odot M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}\odot M</annotation></semantics></math>. The total proxy loss is decomposable into independent subproblems for each matrix block <math id="A3.SSx3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math>, as shown in Equation <a href="#A2.E5" title="In B.1 The Sparse Core Update Step in Depth ‣ Appendix B ARMOR Optimization Algorithm in Depth ‣ ARMOR: High-Performance Semi-Structured Pruning via Adaptive Matrix Factorization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta)=\sum_{i=1}^{d_{\mathrm{out}}/d_{\mathrm{block}}}\sum_{j=1}^{d_{\mathrm{in}}/d_{\mathrm{block}}}||\overline{W}^{(i,j)}-A^{(i)}((W^{\prime}\odot M)^{(i,j)})B^{(j)}||_{F,\text{diag}(XX^{T})^{(j)}}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub></mrow></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta)=\sum_{i=1}^{d_{\mathrm{out}}/d_{\mathrm{block}}}\sum_{j=1}^{d_{\mathrm{in}}/d_{\mathrm{block}}}||\overline{W}^{(i,j)}-A^{(i)}((W^{\prime}\odot M)^{(i,j)})B^{(j)}||_{F,\text{diag}(XX^{T})^{(j)}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SSx3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">The algorithm updates a single 2:4 sparse group <math id="A3.SSx3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i^{\prime},k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i^{\prime},k)</annotation></semantics></math> within each block <math id="A3.SSx3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math>. Let’s focus on one such update. Let the loss before the update for this specific group be <math id="A3.SSx3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{before}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{before}</annotation></semantics></math>. The current mask for this group is <math id="A3.SSx3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{old}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{old}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is one of the <math id="A3.SSx3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{4}{2}=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{4}{2}=6</annotation></semantics></math> possible masks.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SSx3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SSx3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The algorithm proceeds as follows:</span></p>
<ol id="A3.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each of the 6 possible masks <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> in the set of valid masks <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, it calculates the optimal weights <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{m}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{m}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> that minimize the loss for that group, assuming that mask <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen (Equation <a href="#A2.E8" title="In Optimizing the Sparse Group ‣ B.1 The Sparse Core Update Step in Depth ‣ Appendix B ARMOR Optimization Algorithm in Depth ‣ ARMOR: High-Performance Semi-Structured Pruning via Adaptive Matrix Factorization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>). This results in the best possible loss <math id="A3.I4.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{m}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>l</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{m}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> for that mask choice (Equation <a href="#A2.E7" title="In Optimizing the Sparse Group ‣ B.1 The Sparse Core Update Step in Depth ‣ Appendix B ARMOR Optimization Algorithm in Depth ‣ ARMOR: High-Performance Semi-Structured Pruning via Adaptive Matrix Factorization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It then selects the mask <math id="A3.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> that yields the minimum loss among all 6 possibilities: <math id="A3.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{best}=\min_{m\in\mathcal{M}}l_{m}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>l</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{best}=\min_{m\in\mathcal{M}}l_{m}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A3.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The algorithm updates the mask for group <math id="A3.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i^{\prime},k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i^{\prime},k)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and its corresponding weights in <math id="A3.I4.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.I4.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{m^{*}}^{*}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{m^{*}}^{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A3.SSx3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">The loss with the original mask <math id="A3.SSx3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{old}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{old}</annotation></semantics></math> and its weights before the update is <math id="A3.SSx3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{before}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{before}</annotation></semantics></math>. The optimized loss for this original mask, <math id="A3.SSx3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{m_{old}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>l</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{m_{old}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, must be less than or equal to <math id="A3.SSx3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{before}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{before}</annotation></semantics></math>, since Equation 7 finds the optimal weights for any given mask.</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{m_{old}}^{*}\leq l_{before}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>l</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{m_{old}}^{*}\leq l_{before}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SSx3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">By definition, the selected mask <math id="A3.SSx3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the one that minimizes this optimal loss across all 6 choices. Therefore, its loss <math id="A3.SSx3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{best}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{best}</annotation></semantics></math> must be less than or equal to the optimal loss for the old mask <math id="A3.SSx3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{m_{old}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>l</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{m_{old}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{best}\leq l_{m_{old}}^{*}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>l</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{best}\leq l_{m_{old}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SSx3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Combining these, we have <math id="A3.SSx3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{best}\leq l_{before}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{best}\leq l_{before}</annotation></semantics></math>. The update for the selected group can only decrease or maintain the proxy loss. Since this holds for the update in each block, and the block losses are additive, the total proxy loss after the discrete optimization step is guaranteed to be less than or equal to the loss before the step.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SSx4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Proof for Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3.4 Theoretical Results ‣ 3 Methods ‣ ARMOR: High-Performance Semi-Structured Pruning via Adaptive Matrix Factorization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> (Convergence of the ARMOR optimization algorithm)</h3>

<div id="A3.SSx4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SSx4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3.4 Theoretical Results ‣ 3 Methods ‣ ARMOR: High-Performance Semi-Structured Pruning via Adaptive Matrix Factorization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SSx4.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SSx4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SSx4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SSx4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t}=\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((\theta)_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t}=\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((\theta)_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> be the value of the proxy loss at the end of iteration <math id="A3.SSx4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Each iteration of the ARMOR optimization algorithm consists of a continuous optimization step followed by a discrete optimization step.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SSx4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SSx4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">From Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1. ‣ Proof for Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ ARMOR: High-Performance Semi-Structured Pruning via Adaptive Matrix Factorization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, the continuous step does not increase the loss. Let the loss after the continuous step at iteration <math id="A3.SSx4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="A3.SSx4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t+1|cont}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t+1|cont}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t+1|cont}\leq L_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t+1|cont}\leq L_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SSx4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">From Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma C.2. ‣ Proof for Lemma ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ ARMOR: High-Performance Semi-Structured Pruning via Adaptive Matrix Factorization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>, the sparse core step, which follows the continuous step, also does not increase the loss. Let the loss after the discrete step be <math id="A3.SSx4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t+1}\leq L_{t+1|cont}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t+1}\leq L_{t+1|cont}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SSx4.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx4.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Combining these two results gives:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t+1}\leq L_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t+1}\leq L_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SSx4.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx4.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">This shows that the sequence of proxy losses <math id="A3.SSx4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{L_{t}\}_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{L_{t}\}_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> is monotonically non-increasing. By induction, this implies that for any <math id="A3.SSx4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SSx4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t}\leq L_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t}\leq L_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SSx4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SSx4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Furthermore, from Proposition <a href="#Thmprop1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ Proof for Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ ARMOR: High-Performance Semi-Structured Pruning via Adaptive Matrix Factorization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the proxy loss is bounded below by 0. Therefore, <math id="A3.SSx4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{L_{t}\}_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{L_{t}\}_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> is a monotonically non-increasing sequence that is bounded below. By the Monotone Convergence Theorem, any such sequence must converge to a limit.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SSx4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SSx4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SSx4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, the sequence <math id="A3.SSx4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((\theta)_{t})\}_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{L}_{W,X}((\theta)_{t})\}_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> converges, and its value is always less than or equal to its initial value.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Beta Smoothness of Proxy Loss</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we present the proofs that the proxy loss is <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth with respect to each of the parameters <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. And using them, derive the learning rates for the sequential gradient descent based continous optimization step.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Proxy Loss <math id="A4.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth With Respect to <math id="A4.SS1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First let us consider the <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothness of the proxy loss for block <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(i\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(i\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have that:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}\left(\theta^{\left(i,j\right)}\right)=\left\lVert\bar{W}^{\left(i,j\right)}-A^{\left(i\right)}(M^{\left(i,j\right)}\odot W^{\prime\left(i,j\right)})B^{\left(j\right)}\right\rVert_{F,\mathrm{diag}\left(XX^{T}\right)^{\left(j\right)}}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}\left(\theta^{\left(i,j\right)}\right)=\left\lVert\bar{W}^{\left(i,j\right)}-A^{\left(i\right)}(M^{\left(i,j\right)}\odot W^{\prime\left(i,j\right)})B^{\left(j\right)}\right\rVert_{F,\mathrm{diag}\left(XX^{T}\right)^{\left(j\right)}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Where <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\left(i,j\right)}=(A^{\left(i\right)},B^{\left(j\right)},W^{\prime\left(i,j\right)},M^{\left(i,j\right)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\left(i,j\right)}=(A^{\left(i\right)},B^{\left(j\right)},W^{\prime\left(i,j\right)},M^{\left(i,j\right)})</annotation></semantics></math>. We have that:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{A^{\left(i\right)}}\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}\left(\theta^{\left(i,j\right)}\right)=2A^{\left(i\right)}\left(S^{\left(i,j\right)}D^{\left(j\right)}S^{\left(i,j\right)T}\right)-2\bar{W}^{\left(i,j\right)}D^{\left(j\right)}S^{\left(i,j\right)T}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{A^{\left(i\right)}}\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}\left(\theta^{\left(i,j\right)}\right)=2A^{\left(i\right)}\left(S^{\left(i,j\right)}D^{\left(j\right)}S^{\left(i,j\right)T}\right)-2\bar{W}^{\left(i,j\right)}D^{\left(j\right)}S^{\left(i,j\right)T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Where <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\left(i,j\right)}=(M^{\left(i,j\right)}\odot W^{\prime\left(i,j\right)})B^{\left(j\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\left(i,j\right)}=(M^{\left(i,j\right)}\odot W^{\prime\left(i,j\right)})B^{\left(j\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\left(j\right)}=\mathrm{diag}\left(XX^{T}\right)^{\left(j\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\left(j\right)}=\mathrm{diag}\left(XX^{T}\right)^{\left(j\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consdier two <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{(1)},A_{(2)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{block}}\times d_{\mathrm{block}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{(1)},A_{(2)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{block}}\times d_{\mathrm{block}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us denote <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\left(i,j\right)}_{(1)}=(A^{\left(i\right)}_{(1)},B^{\left(j\right)},W^{\prime\left(i,j\right)},M^{\left(i,j\right)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\left(i,j\right)}_{(1)}=(A^{\left(i\right)}_{(1)},B^{\left(j\right)},W^{\prime\left(i,j\right)},M^{\left(i,j\right)})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\left(i,j\right)}_{(2)}=(A^{\left(i\right)}_{(2)},B^{\left(j\right)},W^{\prime\left(i,j\right)},M^{\left(i,j\right)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\left(i,j\right)}_{(2)}=(A^{\left(i\right)}_{(2)},B^{\left(j\right)},W^{\prime\left(i,j\right)},M^{\left(i,j\right)})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have that:
Then we have that:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lVert\nabla_{A^{\left(i\right)}}\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}(\theta^{\left(i,j\right)}_{(1)})-\nabla_{A^{\left(i\right)}}\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}(\theta^{\left(i,j\right)}_{(2)})\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lVert\nabla_{A^{\left(i\right)}}\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}(\theta^{\left(i,j\right)}_{(1)})-\nabla_{A^{\left(i\right)}}\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}(\theta^{\left(i,j\right)}_{(2)})\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\left\lVert\left(A^{\left(i\right)}_{(1)}-A^{\prime\left(i\right)}_{(2)}\right)\left(S^{\left(i,j\right)}D^{\left(j\right)}S^{\left(i,j\right)T}\right)\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\left\lVert\left(A^{\left(i\right)}_{(1)}-A^{\prime\left(i\right)}_{(2)}\right)\left(S^{\left(i,j\right)}D^{\left(j\right)}S^{\left(i,j\right)T}\right)\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\left\lVert A^{\left(i\right)}_{(1)}-A^{\prime\left(i\right)}_{(2)}\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert S^{\left(i,j\right)}D^{\left(j\right)}S^{\left(i,j\right)T}\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\left\lVert A^{\left(i\right)}_{(1)}-A^{\prime\left(i\right)}_{(2)}\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert S^{\left(i,j\right)}D^{\left(j\right)}S^{\left(i,j\right)T}\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Where the inequality follows from the submultiplicativity of the Frobenius norm. Thus we have that the proxy loss <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}(\theta^{\left(i,j\right)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}(\theta^{\left(i,j\right)})</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth with respect to <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\left(i\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\left(i\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{A}^{\left(i,j\right)}=2\left\lVert S^{\left(i,j\right)}D^{\left(j\right)}S^{\left(i,j\right)T}\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{A}^{\left(i,j\right)}=2\left\lVert S^{\left(i,j\right)}D^{\left(j\right)}S^{\left(i,j\right)T}\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. We now consider the overall proxy loss, for some <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{(1)},A_{(2)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{out}}\times d_{\mathrm{in}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{(1)},A_{(2)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{out}}\times d_{\mathrm{in}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{(1)}=(A_{(1)},B,W^{\prime},M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{(1)}=(A_{(1)},B,W^{\prime},M)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{(2)}=(A_{(2)},B,W^{\prime},M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{(2)}=(A_{(2)},B,W^{\prime},M)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have that:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lVert\nabla_{A}\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta_{(1)})-\nabla_{A}\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta_{(2)})\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>A</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>A</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lVert\nabla_{A}\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta_{(1)})-\nabla_{A}\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta_{(2)})\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\lVert\sum_{i=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{out}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\sum_{j=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{in}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\nabla_{A^{\left(i\right)}}\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}(\theta_{(1)}^{\left(i,j\right)})-\nabla_{A^{\left(i\right)}}\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}(\theta_{(2)}^{\left(i,j\right)})\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub></mfrac></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub></mfrac></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\lVert\sum_{i=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{out}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\sum_{j=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{in}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\nabla_{A^{\left(i\right)}}\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}(\theta_{(1)}^{\left(i,j\right)})-\nabla_{A^{\left(i\right)}}\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}(\theta_{(2)}^{\left(i,j\right)})\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{i=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{out}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\sum_{j=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{in}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\left\lVert\nabla_{A^{\left(i\right)}}\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}(\theta^{\left(i,j\right)}_{(1)})-\nabla_{A^{\left(i\right)}}\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}(\theta_{(2)}^{\left(i,j\right)})\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub></mfrac></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub></mfrac></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{i=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{out}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\sum_{j=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{in}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\left\lVert\nabla_{A^{\left(i\right)}}\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}(\theta^{\left(i,j\right)}_{(1)})-\nabla_{A^{\left(i\right)}}\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}(\theta_{(2)}^{\left(i,j\right)})\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\left\lVert A_{(1)}-A_{(2)}\right\rVert_{F}\sum_{i=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{out}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\sum_{j=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{in}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\left\lVert S^{\left(i,j\right)}D^{\left(j\right)}S^{\left(i,j\right)T}\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub></mfrac></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub></mfrac></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\left\lVert A_{(1)}-A_{(2)}\right\rVert_{F}\sum_{i=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{out}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\sum_{j=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{in}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\left\lVert S^{\left(i,j\right)}D^{\left(j\right)}S^{\left(i,j\right)T}\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Where the first inequality follows from the triangle inequality and the second follows from the previous result. Therefore the overall loss <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth with respect to <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{A}=2\sum_{i=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{out}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\sum_{j=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{in}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\left\lVert S^{\left(i,j\right)}D^{\left(j\right)}S^{\left(i,j\right)T}\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub></mfrac></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub></mfrac></msubsup><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{A}=2\sum_{i=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{out}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\sum_{j=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{in}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\left\lVert S^{\left(i,j\right)}D^{\left(j\right)}S^{\left(i,j\right)T}\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. This leads us to a learning rate of:</p>
<table id="A4.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{A}=\frac{1}{\beta_{A}}=\frac{1}{2\sum_{i=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{out}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\sum_{j=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{in}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\left\lVert S^{\left(i,j\right)}D^{\left(j\right)}S^{\left(i,j\right)T}\right\rVert_{F}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub></mfrac></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub></mfrac></msubsup><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{A}=\frac{1}{\beta_{A}}=\frac{1}{2\sum_{i=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{out}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\sum_{j=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{in}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\left\lVert S^{\left(i,j\right)}D^{\left(j\right)}S^{\left(i,j\right)T}\right\rVert_{F}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Proxy Loss <math id="A4.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth With Respect to <math id="A4.SS2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Once again, we start by considering the <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothness of the proxy loss for block <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{\left(j\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{\left(j\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Reusing the notation we introduced in section, we have that:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{B^{\left(j\right)}}\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}(\theta^{\left(i,j\right)})=2S^{\prime\left(i,j\right)T}S^{\left(i,j\right)}B^{\left(j\right)}D^{\left(j\right)}-2S^{\prime\left(i,j\right)T}\bar{W}^{\left(i,j\right)}D^{\left(j\right)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{B^{\left(j\right)}}\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}(\theta^{\left(i,j\right)})=2S^{\prime\left(i,j\right)T}S^{\left(i,j\right)}B^{\left(j\right)}D^{\left(j\right)}-2S^{\prime\left(i,j\right)T}\bar{W}^{\left(i,j\right)}D^{\left(j\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Where <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime\left(i,j\right)}=A^{\left(i\right)}(M^{\left(i,j\right)}\odot W^{\prime\left(i,j\right)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime\left(i,j\right)}=A^{\left(i\right)}(M^{\left(i,j\right)}\odot W^{\prime\left(i,j\right)})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\left(j\right)}=\mathrm{diag}\left(XX^{T}\right)^{\left(j\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\left(j\right)}=\mathrm{diag}\left(XX^{T}\right)^{\left(j\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consdier two <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{(1)},B_{(2)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{block}}\times d_{\mathrm{block}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{(1)},B_{(2)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{block}}\times d_{\mathrm{block}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us denote <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\left(i,j\right)}_{(1)}=(A^{\left(i\right)},B^{\left(j\right)}_{(1)},W^{\prime\left(i,j\right)},M^{\left(i,j\right)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\left(i,j\right)}_{(1)}=(A^{\left(i\right)},B^{\left(j\right)}_{(1)},W^{\prime\left(i,j\right)},M^{\left(i,j\right)})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\left(i,j\right)}_{(2)}=(A^{\left(i\right)},B^{\left(j\right)}_{(2)},W^{\prime\left(i,j\right)},M^{\left(i,j\right)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\left(i,j\right)}_{(2)}=(A^{\left(i\right)},B^{\left(j\right)}_{(2)},W^{\prime\left(i,j\right)},M^{\left(i,j\right)})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have that:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lVert\nabla_{B^{\left(j\right)}}\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}(\theta^{\left(i,j\right)}_{(1)})-\nabla_{B^{\left(j\right)}}\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}(\theta_{(2)}^{\left(i,j\right)})\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lVert\nabla_{B^{\left(j\right)}}\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}(\theta^{\left(i,j\right)}_{(1)})-\nabla_{B^{\left(j\right)}}\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}(\theta_{(2)}^{\left(i,j\right)})\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\left\lVert S^{\prime\left(i,j\right)T}S^{\left(i,j\right)}\left(B^{\left(j\right)}_{(1)}-B^{\left(j\right)}_{(2)}\right)D^{\left(j\right)}\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\left\lVert S^{\prime\left(i,j\right)T}S^{\left(i,j\right)}\left(B^{\left(j\right)}_{(1)}-B^{\left(j\right)}_{(2)}\right)D^{\left(j\right)}\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\left\lVert S^{\prime\left(i,j\right)T}S^{\left(i,j\right)}\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert B^{\left(j\right)}_{(1)}-B^{\left(j\right)}_{(2)}\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert D^{\left(j\right)}\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\left\lVert S^{\prime\left(i,j\right)T}S^{\left(i,j\right)}\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert B^{\left(j\right)}_{(1)}-B^{\left(j\right)}_{(2)}\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert D^{\left(j\right)}\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Where the inequality follows from the submultiplicativity of the Frobenius norm. Thus we have that the proxy loss <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}(\theta^{\left(i,j\right)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}(\theta^{\left(i,j\right)})</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth with respect to <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{\left(j\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{\left(j\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{B}^{\left(i,j\right)}=2\left\lVert S^{\prime\left(i,j\right)T}S^{\prime\left(i,j\right)}\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert D^{\left(j\right)}\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{B}^{\left(i,j\right)}=2\left\lVert S^{\prime\left(i,j\right)T}S^{\prime\left(i,j\right)}\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert D^{\left(j\right)}\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. Following the same procedure as the <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> case, consider some <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{(1)},B_{(2)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{in}}\times d_{\mathrm{in}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{(1)},B_{(2)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{in}}\times d_{\mathrm{in}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{(1)}=(A,B_{(1)},W^{\prime},M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{(1)}=(A,B_{(1)},W^{\prime},M)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{(2)}=(A,B_{(2)},W^{\prime},M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{(2)}=(A,B_{(2)},W^{\prime},M)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have that for the overall proxy loss:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\nabla_{B}\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta_{(1)})-\nabla_{B}\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta_{(2)})\right\rVert_{F}\leq 2\left\lVert B_{(1)}-B_{(2)}\right\rVert_{F}\sum_{i=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{out}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\sum_{j=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{in}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\left\lVert S^{\prime\left(i,j\right)T}S^{\left(i,j\right)}\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert D^{\left(j\right)}\right\rVert_{F}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>B</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>B</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub></mfrac></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub></mfrac></munderover><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\nabla_{B}\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta_{(1)})-\nabla_{B}\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta_{(2)})\right\rVert_{F}\leq 2\left\lVert B_{(1)}-B_{(2)}\right\rVert_{F}\sum_{i=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{out}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\sum_{j=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{in}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\left\lVert S^{\prime\left(i,j\right)T}S^{\left(i,j\right)}\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert D^{\left(j\right)}\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Therefore the overall loss <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth with respect to <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{B}=2\sum_{i=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{out}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\sum_{j=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{in}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\left\lVert S^{\prime\left(i,j\right)T}S^{\left(i,j\right)}\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert D^{\left(j\right)}\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub></mfrac></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub></mfrac></msubsup><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{B}=2\sum_{i=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{out}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\sum_{j=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{in}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\left\lVert S^{\prime\left(i,j\right)T}S^{\left(i,j\right)}\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert D^{\left(j\right)}\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. This leads us to a learning rate of:</p>
<table id="A4.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{B}=\frac{1}{\beta_{B}}=\frac{1}{2\sum_{i=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{out}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\sum_{j=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{in}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\left\lVert S^{\prime\left(i,j\right)T}S^{\left(i,j\right)}\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert D^{\left(j\right)}\right\rVert_{F}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub></mfrac></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub></mfrac></msubsup><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{B}=\frac{1}{\beta_{B}}=\frac{1}{2\sum_{i=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{out}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\sum_{j=1}^{\frac{d_{\mathrm{in}}}{d_{\mathrm{block}}}}\left\lVert S^{\prime\left(i,j\right)T}S^{\left(i,j\right)}\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert D^{\left(j\right)}\right\rVert_{F}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Proxy Loss <math id="A4.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth With Respect to <math id="A4.SS3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we consider the <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothness of the proxy loss with respect to <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have that:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{W^{\prime}}\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta)=\left(2A^{T}A(W^{\prime}\odot M)B\mathrm{diag}\left(XX^{T}\right)B^{T}-2A^{T}\bar{W}\mathrm{diag}\left(XX^{T}\right)B^{T}\right)\odot M" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{W^{\prime}}\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta)=\left(2A^{T}A(W^{\prime}\odot M)B\mathrm{diag}\left(XX^{T}\right)B^{T}-2A^{T}\bar{W}\mathrm{diag}\left(XX^{T}\right)B^{T}\right)\odot M</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Consdier two <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}_{(1)},W^{\prime}_{(2)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{out}}\times d_{\mathrm{in}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}_{(1)},W^{\prime}_{(2)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{out}}\times d_{\mathrm{in}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us denote <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{(1)}=(A,B,W^{\prime}_{(1)},M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{(1)}=(A,B,W^{\prime}_{(1)},M)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{(2)}=(A,B,W^{\prime}_{(2)},M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{(2)}=(A,B,W^{\prime}_{(2)},M)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have that:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\lVert\nabla_{W^{\prime}}\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta_{(1)})-\nabla_{W^{\prime}}\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta_{(2)})\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\lVert\nabla_{W^{\prime}}\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta_{(1)})-\nabla_{W^{\prime}}\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta_{(2)})\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\left\lVert\left(A^{T}A\left((W^{\prime}_{(1)}-W^{\prime}_{(2)})\odot M\right)B\mathrm{diag}\left(XX^{T}\right)B^{T}\right)\odot M\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\left\lVert\left(A^{T}A\left((W^{\prime}_{(1)}-W^{\prime}_{(2)})\odot M\right)B\mathrm{diag}\left(XX^{T}\right)B^{T}\right)\odot M\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\left\lVert A^{T}A\left((W^{\prime}_{(1)}-W^{\prime}_{(2)})\odot M\right)B\mathrm{diag}\left(XX^{T}\right)B^{T}\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\left\lVert A^{T}A\left((W^{\prime}_{(1)}-W^{\prime}_{(2)})\odot M\right)B\mathrm{diag}\left(XX^{T}\right)B^{T}\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\left\lVert A^{T}A\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert B\mathrm{diag}\left(XX^{T}\right)B^{T}\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert(W^{\prime}_{(1)}-W^{\prime}_{(2)})\odot M\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\left\lVert A^{T}A\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert B\mathrm{diag}\left(XX^{T}\right)B^{T}\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert(W^{\prime}_{(1)}-W^{\prime}_{(2)})\odot M\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\left\lVert A^{T}A\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert B\mathrm{diag}\left(XX^{T}\right)B^{T}\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert W^{\prime}_{(1)}-W^{\prime}_{(2)}\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\left\lVert A^{T}A\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert B\mathrm{diag}\left(XX^{T}\right)B^{T}\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert W^{\prime}_{(1)}-W^{\prime}_{(2)}\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Where the first and third inequalities follow from the property that <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert V\odot M\right\rVert_{F}\leq\left\lVert M\right\rVert_{\mathrm{max}}\left\lVert V\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert V\odot M\right\rVert_{F}\leq\left\lVert M\right\rVert_{\mathrm{max}}\left\lVert V\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> for any matrices <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V,M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V,M</annotation></semantics></math> of the same shape, and the second follows from the submultiplicativity of the Frobenius norm. Thus we have that the proxy loss <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{W,X}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth with respect to <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{W^{\prime}}=2\left\lVert A^{T}A\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert B\mathrm{diag}\left(XX^{T}\right)B^{T}\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{W^{\prime}}=2\left\lVert A^{T}A\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert B\mathrm{diag}\left(XX^{T}\right)B^{T}\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. This leads us to a learning rate of:</p>
<table id="A4.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{W^{\prime}}=\frac{1}{\beta_{W^{\prime}}}=\frac{1}{2\left\lVert A^{T}A\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert B\mathrm{diag}\left(XX^{T}\right)B^{T}\right\rVert_{F}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>β</mi><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diag</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{W^{\prime}}=\frac{1}{\beta_{W^{\prime}}}=\frac{1}{2\left\lVert A^{T}A\right\rVert_{F}\left\lVert B\mathrm{diag}\left(XX^{T}\right)B^{T}\right\rVert_{F}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Ablations</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Selection Heuristic</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We investigated four choices for the sparse group selection heuristic used in the Discrete Optimization steps:</p>
<ul id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Uniform Random Selection (Random)</span>. We select a sparse group from the available <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{block}}^{2}/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{block}}^{2}/4</annotation></semantics></math> sparse groups within a sparse core block.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">L1 Greedy Selection</span>, We directly select the sparse group based on which group has the maximum L1 gradient norm.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">L2 Random Selection</span>, We draw a sparse group with probability that is based on the L2 norm of the gradient, instead of the L1 norm:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(i,j)}_{(i^{\prime},k)}\propto\left\lVert\nabla_{{\left(M\odot W^{\prime}\right)^{\left(i,j\right)}}_{i^{\prime},\left[k\right]}}\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}\right\rVert_{2}\quad\forall\quad i^{\prime}\in[d_{\mathrm{block}}],\quad k\in[d_{\mathrm{block}}/4]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∝</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mmultiscripts><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mo>∀</mo><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>block</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(i,j)}_{(i^{\prime},k)}\propto\left\lVert\nabla_{{\left(M\odot W^{\prime}\right)^{\left(i,j\right)}}_{i^{\prime},\left[k\right]}}\ell_{X}^{(i,j)}\right\rVert_{2}\quad\forall\quad i^{\prime}\in[d_{\mathrm{block}}],\quad k\in[d_{\mathrm{block}}/4].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">L1 Random Selection</span>, This is the selection heuristic discussed in the main text and that we use.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The results of this ablation is listed in table <a href="#A5.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ E.1 Selection Heuristic ‣ Appendix E Ablations ‣ ARMOR: High-Performance Semi-Structured Pruning via Adaptive Matrix Factorization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. L1 random and L2 random perform roughly equivalently.</p>
</div>
